@startuml neural-modernbert-architecture
' ModernBERT-base as libgrammstein drives it: BPE tokenizer → RoPE token embeddings →
' 22 pre-norm GeGLU layers with alternating local/global attention → final norm, then the
' two exits the wrapper exposes: (a) pooled sentence vector, (b) MLM vocabulary logits
' through the replicated head + tied decoder.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/neural-modernbert-architecture.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/neural/model.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title ModernBERT-base — encoder stack and the two exits used by libgrammstein

rectangle "**Input text**\n“The quick brown fox”" as text #546E7A

rectangle "**Tokenizer** (BPE, 50 368 types)\nencode(text, add_special = true)\n⟶ [CLS] · sub-words · [SEP]" as tok #2E7D32

rectangle "**Token embeddings** + LayerNorm\nE ∈ ℝ^(V × H),  H = 768\nno absolute positions · no token-type IDs" as emb #2E7D32

rectangle "**Encoder — 22 pre-norm layers**\nattention: RoPE-rotated Q·Kᵀ\nlayer ℓ global ⟺ ℓ mod 3 = 0\nother layers: sliding window (±64)\nMLP: GeGLU, intermediate 1 152" as enc #2E7D32

rectangle "**final_norm**\nhidden states  H ∈ ℝ^(B × T × 768)" as hid #2E7D32

rectangle "**Pooling**\nCLS: h₀      mean: (1/T) Σₜ hₜ" as pool #2E7D32
rectangle "**Sentence vector**\nℝ^768  (optionally ℓ₂-normalized)" as vec #2E7D32

rectangle "**MLM head** (replicated)\nDense(768→768) → GELU(erf) → LayerNorm" as head #2E7D32
rectangle "**Decoder** (weights tied to E)\nz = Eᵀ·x + b   ⟶  ℝ^(B × T × 50 368)" as dec #2E7D32
rectangle "**Vocabulary logits**\nlog-softmax ⟶ log ℙ(token | context)" as logits #2E7D32

text --> tok
tok --> emb : token IDs (u32)
emb --> enc
enc --> hid

hid --> pool : embed / embed_mean_pooled
pool --> vec

hid --> head : get_mlm_logits
head --> dec
dec --> logits

note right of enc #E8F5E9
  Local–global alternation is what buys the
  8 192-token window: only ⌈22/3⌉ = 8 layers pay
  the quadratic Θ(T²·H) attention bill; the other
  14 pay Θ(T·w·H) with window w = 128.
end note

note right of head #E8F5E9
  candle's ModernBertHead / ModernBertDecoder have
  private constructors, and ModernBertForMaskedLM
  hides its own encoder. libgrammstein therefore
  rebuilds both from the //same// VarBuilder — weight
  paths head.dense, head.norm,
  model.embeddings.tok_embeddings.weight, decoder.bias
  — so one 149 M-parameter encoder serves both exits.
end note

@enduml
